\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. PLEASANT are Thy courts above,
\par In the land of light and love;
\par Pleasant are Thy courts below,
\par In this land of sin and woe.
\par O my spirit longs and faints
\par For the converse of Thy saints,
\par For the brightness of Thy face,
\par For Thy fullness, God of grace!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Happy birds that sing and fly
\par Round Thy alters, O most high !
\par Happier souls that find a rest 
\par In a heavenly Father's breast !
\par Like the wandering dove that found
\par No repose on earth around, 
\par They can to their ark repair,
\par And enjoy it ever there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Happy souls! Their praises flow
\par In this vale of sin and woe;
\par Waters in the desert rise,
\par Manna feeds them from the skies.
\par On they go from strength to strength,
\par Till they reach Thy throne at length;
\par At Thy feet adoring fall,
\par Who hast led them safe through all.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, be mine this prize to win:
\par Guide me through a world of sin;
\par Keep me by Thy saving grace;
\par Give me at Thy side a place.
\par Sun and shield alike Thou art ;
\par Guide and guard my erring heart:
\par Grace and glory flow from Thee;
\par Shower, O shower them, Lord, on me !     
\par                                            AMEN.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang1040\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

